% ============================================================================
% soil-horizons.query.adj — a worked recall over the earth-science
% soil-horizons library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what is the C horizon made
% of?": it states no soil-science fact of its own — it only `import`s the
% grounded table and asks binding queries. The engine resolves each `?` against
% the `horizon_material` rows and returns the material + the table's source/
% locator/trust. The fourth query runs the relation BACKWARD (bind the material
% `bedrock`, recall its horizon — r). A word that is not one of the master
% horizons abstains honestly — the engine never invents a material.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli soil-horizons.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "soil-horizons.adj"

? horizon_material(o, $Material)        % expect organic_matter
? horizon_material(c, $Material)        % expect parent_material
? horizon_material(r, $Material)        % expect bedrock
? horizon_material($Horizon, bedrock)   % reverse bind — expect r
? horizon_material(humus, $Material)    % expect abstain — humus is a component of soil organic matter, not one of the master horizons
